      equipment: 'Standard pack, score pad or chips.',
      dealing: 'Deal nine cards face-down to each player. Players then divide their hand into three separate 3-card Brag combinations.',
    },
    turnFlow: '1. **Partition**: Players divide 9 cards into Hand 1, Hand 2, and Hand 3. 2. **Ordering**: Some variants require hands to be ordered from strongest to weakest. 3. **Comparison**: Hands are revealed one at a time. The winner of each comparison (e.g., Hand 1 vs. Hand 1) scores a point. 4. **Ranks**: Prial (3-3-3 is highest) > Running Flush > Run > Flush > Pair > High Card.',
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: '9-Card Brag is typically scored via points per hand rather than using a monetary ante system.',
      deal: 'The initial distribution of nine cards to all players is performed automatically by the system dealer.',
      reveal_market: 'This is a closed-hand partition game where all cards are held privately; no shared market exists.',
      buy_market: 'Players cannot purchase cards from a market; hand strength is fixed after the initial deal.',
      buy_stock: 'The entire hand is distributed at the start; no drawing or buying from the stock is permitted during play.',
      fold: 'Players must participate in all hand comparisons to determine the final point tally for the round.',
      check: 'The game uses a partition and reveal structure rather than a vying structure with checks and bets.',
      call: 'There is no pot or bet to match in this variant; competition is based on hand strength comparisons.',
      bet: 'Success is measured by points earned in individual comparisons rather than through wagering of assets.',
      raise: 'The value of the deal is fixed by game rules and cannot be raised through wagering rounds.',
      declare: 'Hand results are established during the showdown comparison rather than through a formal declaration.',
      reveal_hand: 'Hands remain private until the system triggers the comparison logic at the end of the partition phase.',
      award_pot: 'Winning results in point accumulation on a scorecard rather than distributing a physical pot of chips.',
      play_card: '9-Card Brag is a partition game where hands are compared rather than played to individual tricks.',
      draw: 'Each player receives nine cards at the start and no further drawing occurs during the play of the hand.',
      discard: 'Every card in the nine-card deal must be partitioned into the three hands; no cards are discarded.',
      pass: 'Players must always provide a complete partition of their hand; passing a turn is not supported.',
      bid: 'Bidding is not used in the point-scoring version of 9-Card Brag; game objectives are fixed.',
      meld: 'Hand resolution is based strictly on three-card poker hierarchies rather than forming melds.',
      go_out: 'The hand terminates only after all three comparisons have been performed by the system dealer.',
    },
