      'Turn-flow example: 1. **Partition**: Players divide 9 cards into Hand 1, Hand 2, and Hand 3. 2. **Ordering**: Some variants require hands to be ordered from strongest to weakest. 3. **Comparison**: Hands are revealed one at a time. The winner of each comparison (e.g., Hand 1 vs. Hand 1) scores a point. 4. **Ranks**: Prial (3-3-3 is highest) > Running Flush > Run > Flush > Pair > High Card.',
      'Scoring example: Points are awarded for each winning hand comparison. Bonus points for winning all three (the Crash). Win the majority of hand comparisons in the round..',
